# Xcode Build & Test

**NEVER** use `swift test` or `swift build` — SwiftData macros require the Xcode build system. Always use `xcodebuild`.

**DEVELOPER_DIR** must point to `~/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer` because `xcode-select` is set to Command Line Tools, not full Xcode. **Always** prefix every `xcodebuild` call with this environment variable.

The validated toolchain is **Xcode 27.0 build 27A5209h**. `.xcode-version`
pins the marketing version only; before recording snapshots, confirm the exact
build with `xcodebuild -version`. Update this baseline deliberately when the
beta or final Xcode build changes.

For SPM package tests, also add `PATH="/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin:$PATH"` so `simctl` is found.

## Build

```bash
set -o pipefail
cd ~/Documents/repo/FitnessApp && DEVELOPER_DIR=/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer xcodebuild build -scheme FitnessApp -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro Max,OS=26.0' 2>&1 | tail -30
```

## Unit Tests

All unit tests live in SPM packages — there is no app-level `FitnessAppTests` target. Use the "Package Tests" section below to run them without building the app.

## UI Tests

UI tests **must** use the dedicated `FitnessApp UITests` scheme. That scheme builds with the `UITesting` configuration which defines the `UITESTING` Swift compilation flag — without it, `UITestLaunchStrategy` (and the entire `--uitesting` argument path in `FitnessAppApp.swift`) is compiled out and the app boots with production data, so tests fail in non-obvious ways (e.g. selectors not found because the seeded fixture screen never appears). The plain `FitnessApp` scheme uses the `Debug` configuration and does **not** define `UITESTING`.

```bash
set -o pipefail
cd ~/Documents/repo/FitnessApp && DEVELOPER_DIR=/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer xcodebuild test -scheme "FitnessApp UITests" -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro Max,OS=26.0' -only-testing:FitnessAppUITests 2>&1 | tail -30
```

## Package Tests (SPM)

SPM test targets are **not** in the app scheme. Run them via the **package's own scheme** from the package directory. Always add `-skipMacroValidation` (required for swift-testing macros).

### Single package

```bash
set -o pipefail
cd ~/Documents/repo/FitnessApp/Packages/FitnessTraining && DEVELOPER_DIR=/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer PATH="/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin:$PATH" xcodebuild test -scheme FitnessTraining-Package -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro Max,OS=26.0' -skipMacroValidation 2>&1 | tail -30
```

### All packages (sequential — for CI / debugging a single failure)

```bash
set -o pipefail
fail=0
for pkg in FitnessExercise FitnessTraining FitnessAnalytics FitnessStorage FitnessProfile; do
 echo "=== Testing $pkg ==="
 cd ~/Documents/repo/FitnessApp/Packages/$pkg || exit 1
 scheme=$pkg
 if [ "$pkg" = "FitnessTraining" ]; then scheme=FitnessTraining-Package; fi
 if ! DEVELOPER_DIR=/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer PATH="/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin:$PATH" xcodebuild test -scheme $scheme -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro Max,OS=26.0' -skipMacroValidation 2>&1 | tail -10; then fail=1; fi
done
exit $fail
```

### Fast Test Loop (parallel — for local dev)

The bottleneck when running multiple package schemes is not test execution — it's the `xcodebuild` process startup + simulator attach overhead (≈4 s per scheme). Running each scheme as an independent background shell reduces total wall-clock from ~34 s to ~8 s on an iPhone 17 Pro Max simulator with the current suite.

Boot the simulator once, then run all packages in parallel. The simulator serialises concurrent test runners internally, so this is safe.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# Save as scripts/fast-test.sh
set -u
export DEVELOPER_DIR=/Users/jose.nunez/Downloads/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer
export PATH="$DEVELOPER_DIR/usr/bin:$PATH"

PACKAGES=(FitnessExercise FitnessTraining FitnessAnalytics FitnessStorage FitnessProfile FitnessWorkouts)
DEST='platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17 Pro Max,OS=26.0'
LOG_DIR=$(mktemp -d)

# Boot simulator once (no-op if already booted)
xcrun simctl boot 'iPhone 17 Pro Max' 2>/dev/null || true

pids=()
for pkg in "${PACKAGES[@]}"; do
 (
   if ! cd ~/Documents/repo/FitnessApp/Packages/$pkg; then
     echo "1 $pkg" > "$LOG_DIR/$pkg.exit"
     exit 0
   fi
   scheme="$pkg"
   if [ "$pkg" = "FitnessTraining" ]; then scheme="FitnessTraining-Package"; fi
   status=0
   xcodebuild test -scheme "$scheme" -destination "$DEST" -skipMacroValidation \
     > "$LOG_DIR/$pkg.log" 2>&1 || status=$?
   echo "$status $pkg" > "$LOG_DIR/$pkg.exit"
 ) &
 pids+=($!)
done

for pid in "${pids[@]}"; do wait "$pid" || true; done

echo "=== Results ==="
fail=0
for pkg in "${PACKAGES[@]}"; do
 status=$(cut -d' ' -f1 "$LOG_DIR/$pkg.exit")
 if [ "$status" = "0" ]; then
   summary=$(grep -E '^(Test Suite .* passed|\*\* TEST SUCCEEDED \*\*|Executed [0-9]+ tests)' "$LOG_DIR/$pkg.log" | tail -1)
   printf "  OK  %-20s %s\n" "$pkg" "$summary"
 else
   printf "  FAIL %-20s (see $LOG_DIR/$pkg.log)\n" "$pkg"
   fail=1
 fi
done

exit $fail
```

When a package fails, the per-package log in `$LOG_DIR` has the full output. Use the sequential loop above only when debugging a single failure in isolation or when CI memory limits prevent parallel simulators.

## Notes

- **Liquid Glass visual check**: `swift-snapshot-testing` does not capture SwiftUI's post-compositing Liquid Glass effect reliably. When changing `.appGlassEffect` or `.appDarkSurface`, build and inspect the app on iOS 27 before merge: BottomMenuBar, category filter, category tiles, training cards/action bar, and workout cards must retain their dark, non-beveled hierarchy. `.appGlassEffect` uses clear Glass there; `.appDarkSurface` uses the deterministic dark fill and neutral outline. `AdaptiveSurfacePolicyTests.currentPlatformPolicy` verifies the runtime mapping; visual appearance remains a manual runtime check.
- **Scheme**: Use `FitnessApp` for app/UI tests. Most SPM packages use the package name; `FitnessTraining` has multiple products and therefore uses the generated `FitnessTraining-Package` scheme for its test action.
- **Simulator**: `iPhone 17 Pro Max`. Boot it first if needed: `DEVELOPER_DIR=... .../usr/bin/simctl boot <UDID>`
- **OS pin**: Standard destinations pin `OS=26.0`. This is required for **snapshot-test stability** — a floating runtime renders sub-pixel-different antialiasing and silently drifts the recorded baselines. The iOS 26 destination intentionally verifies the app's minimum supported runtime. Never compare one baseline across runtimes. On an intentional Xcode/runtime bump, re-record snapshot baselines in a dedicated commit.
- To run a **single test**, append the test class and method: `-only-testing:FitnessAppUITests/TrainingUITests/testFullTrainingFlow`
- To run **all UI tests**, use: `-only-testing:FitnessAppUITests`
- Set `block_until_ms` to `300000` (5 min) since build + test takes ~90–120 seconds.
- Always add `-skipMacroValidation` when running package tests via CLI.
